IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sa-provisions`

-- Cross-references of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia), version 20.11.2025 (unofficial plain-text rendering).
-- Generated by a script that reads the text file and finds every printed reference from one provision to another:
-- "section N", "section N(n)", "subsection (n)", "subsection (n)(x)", "paragraph (x)", "this section", "this subsection",
-- "that subsection", "this clause", and "the table" where a table is meant, with the provision each points at resolved by rule.
-- A reference to another Act is a row of its own kind, carrying the instrument and provision as printed; it is not resolved here.
-- For each internal row the test asserts that the cited identifier is in the index of sa-provisions.l4
-- and that the row's heading is the heading the index gives for it.

DECLARE `Cross-reference` HAS
    `citing provision`                          IS A STRING
    `words as printed`                          IS A STRING
    `cited provision`                           IS A STRING
    `heading of the cited provision as printed` IS A STRING
    `line in the text file`                     IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Reference to another instrument` HAS
    `citing provision`                       IS A STRING
    `words as printed`                       IS A STRING
    instrument                               IS A STRING
    `provision of the instrument as printed` IS A STRING
    `line in the text file`                  IS A NUMBER

GIVEN reference IS A `Cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cited provision is in the index with the heading the row gives` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision the index gives for` (reference's `cited provision`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST `the entry` THEN `the entry`'s heading EQUALS reference's `heading of the cited provision as printed`

GIVEN reference IS A `Reference to another instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the citing provision of the reference is in the index` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision the index gives for` (reference's `citing provision`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST `the entry` THEN TRUE

